{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794652134,"nonce":"xSF8NG6+WULwCmGYow4sb5jevOw=","message":"What separates nAIR from AIR (user, 2026-11-14): nAIR may carry information HashLink bytecode never gave us. Definition: nAIR is AIR plus enrichment, produced from the Haxe AST.\n\nAIR already goes past the bytecode in places: vector lanes live in ValueData.lanes because the HL type table cannot hold them, and Fma, VecOp, Intrinsic, Assert and Prefetch have no HL opcode. ModuleInfo::intrinsic_of already works by the embedder vouching for a fact. nAIR extends that practice with facts that come from the source.\n\nRules:\n1. nAIR contains AIR. Every function the HL frontend lowers is a valid nAIR function with no enrichment, and every pass stays correct on it. Enrichment only licenses more.\n2. One IR, one verifier, one set of backends and passes. The enrichment rides on values, instructions and the function as optional fields and side tables, so GVN, LICM, SROA, inlining, OSR and the walker are not forked.\n3. A fact is either checkable by the verifier or vouched by the frontend and listed as such, as the intrinsic table is. A wrong fact miscompiles, so each fact gets a debug-build check.\n4. Layout stays HashLink's. nAIR separates the runtime type (an HL type, which fixes layout and ABI) from the static type (what the Haxe source says). The static type is new.\n5. serialize-to-bytecode applies only to the enrichment-free subset.\n\nEnrichment, each landing with the pass that consumes it:\n- Types: pointer or scalar (713cc00), nullability, `Null\u003cT\u003e` versus `T`, generic arguments before erasure, array element type, exact or final class.\n- Values: non-null, immutable, unique or non-escaping, ranges.\n- Calls: known target sets from the closed world, `inline` and `@:pure` hints, per-function summaries (pure, no-throw, no-alloc).\n- Structure: counted loops with their bounds, `for` over an array with bounds known, exhaustive switch over an enum, try regions that cannot throw.\n- Objects and closures: constructor effects at the `new`, capture layout and which captures are mutated, known closure targets.\n- Provenance: source spans and variable names.","files":null}]}